lesson: 206
title: Hooves and horseshoes
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: A horse has 4 legs, and each leg ends in a hoof, so a horse has 4 hooves.
explain: A blacksmith fits one horseshoe on each hoof, so every horse needs 4 horseshoes.
explain: 6 horses, of which 2 already have shoes: 6 − 2 = 4 horses still need shoes, and 4 × 4 = 16 horseshoes.
vars: a=name b=name n=3..12 k=1..9
need: k < n
answer: 4 * (n - k)
exercise: A stable has {n} horses. {k} of them already have new shoes. How many horseshoes does the blacksmith need for the rest?
exercise: {a} has {n} horses on the farm, and {k} were shod last week. How many horseshoes are needed for the others?
exercise: The blacksmith must shoe {n} horses today. He has finished {k} of them. How many more horseshoes will he fit?
exercise: Of {n} ponies at the riding school, {k} have been shod. How many horseshoes are still needed?
exercise: {a} and {b} help at a stable with {n} horses; {k} horses have shoes already. How many horseshoes are needed for the rest?
exercise: {n} horses, {k} done already, how many shoes left to put on
exercise: the farrier's doing {n} horses, did {k} b4 lunch. how many horseshoes this arvo
exercise: {n+1} horses — no {n}, one's been sold — and {k} already got shoes. how many horseshoes still needed
exercise: {a} reckons a horse needs 2 shoes like us lol. {n} horses, {k} already shod, how many shoes then
exercise: riding camp has {n} ponies, {k} got new shoes, rest need them, mum says it costs heaps. how many shoes
test: How many horseshoes will the blacksmith still fit, if {k} of the {n} horses in the yard are already shod?
test: Only {k} horses out of {n} at the show have fresh shoes. Count the horseshoes needed for all the others.
test: {b} brings {n} horses to the blacksmith. The blacksmith says {k} of them are fine. How many horseshoes will the rest need?
test: Every hoof of the horses without shoes gets one. {n} horses stand in the stable and {k} of them already have shoes. How many horseshoes are used?
test: {n} ponies, {k} shod already. shoes needed?
test: farrier coming, {n} horses, {k} don't need doing, the dog's barking at him. how many horseshoes
exam: Determine the number of horseshoes requisite for the shoeing of those horses, among a total of {n.words}, which remain unshod, given that {k.words} have already been shod.
exam: It is given that a stable accommodates {n} horses, of which {k} are already furnished with shoes. Ascertain the quantity of horseshoes to be fitted to the remainder.
exam: A blacksmith is engaged to shoe {n} ponies; {k} have been completed. Compute the number of horseshoes yet to be applied.
exam: Whereas {k} of the {n} horses of a riding establishment have been shod, state the number of horseshoes required in respect of the others.
exercise: The stable had {n+1} horses, but the oldest one 'went to the glue factory'. {k} of the others already have new shoes. How many horseshoes does the blacksmith need for the rest?
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {a} {n} horses; {k} of them had been shod just before. How many horseshoes are needed for the others?
test: {n+1} horses, one got put down last week, rip. {k} already shod. how many shoes for the rest, and keep the bloody farrier out the pub
